_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\nFound in version 4.6.2.stable\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.6.2.stable (71f334935) - Windows 11 (build 26200) - Multi-window, 1 monitor - Direct3D 12 (Forward+) - dedicated Intel(R) Iris(R) Xe Graphics (Intel Corporation; 32.0.101.7084) - 13th Gen Intel(R) Core(TM) i7-1355U (12 threads) - 15.69 GiB memory\n\n### Issue description\n\nWhen using the animation tree tab, specifically in the BlendSpace2D, the side panels get pushed off screen. This only happens when you have added an animation into the blendspace, and have now clicked on it. You cant resize the tab, or zoom out. If you make the window smaller, the side panels are still cut off.\n(Fullscreen screenshot)\n\n<img width=\"1280\" height=\"800\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/c4f44b84-0d96-4070-a530-d5a9473a7676\" />\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nAfter creating an animation tree attached to an animation player, set the tree root to an AnimationNodeBlendSpace2D. Add an animation point into the blendspace, and click on it to edit it. The side panels will then be cut off.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nN/A","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repo